.\n- Support fact filters on route_id, operator, vehicle_group and date.\n- Route attributes route_name, start_stop and end_stop belong to bus_routes and require a join.\n- Group by the selected ds expression.\n- Sort by ds ascending.\n- Generate only one SELECT statement.\n- The source values of operator and vehicle_group may contain leading or trailing whitespace.\n- When filtering by operator, always apply TRIM to the database column: TRIM(d.operator).\n- When filtering by vehicle_group, always apply TRIM to the database column: TRIM(d.vehicle_group).\n- Compare trimmed operator and vehicle_group values using exact equality (=), unless the user explicitly requests partial or pattern matching.\n- route_id, operator and vehicle_group are independent fact filters and may be applied together in the same WHERE clause.\n\n\nRequirements:\n- Follow the supplied schema context and SQL rules.\n- Apply ALL filters in forecast_request.\n- Return exactly two columns: ds and y.\n- Sort ds ascending.\n- Use only described tables and columns.\n- Generate only one SELECT statement; no write or DDL statements.\n\nReturn JSON only:\n{\"status\":\"success\",\"sql\":\"SELECT ...\",\"explanation\":\"short Vietnamese explanation\"}.",
